{"_meta":{"ui":{"resourceUri":"ui://omitly/result-card.html"},"ui/resourceUri":"ui://omitly/result-card.html"},"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Verify document"},"description":"Reports whether a received PDF's embedded Omitly audit report and whole-file seal still verify (v1: Ed25519; v2: ML-DSA-87 with ECDSA P-384) \u2014 on-device, needs the native engine, no licence required. A seal shows integrity, not origin, and is not a check of the content: the signing key travels with the file, so a valid seal means 'unchanged since sealed by the holder of this key', never 'produced by Omitly', and anyone can seal a file with their own key. This tool never gives `safe_to_send`; for the content, run `check_redaction`. A `seal_unsupported_version` verdict means this verifier is too old to check the seal at all; update the verifier rather than trusting or rejecting the file on that basis. `outcome` is the only verdict field; isError false does not mean the file is safe. isError true means the check could not run.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"pdfPath":{"description":"absolute path to the PDF to check for an Omitly audit report and seal","type":"string"}},"required":["pdfPath"],"type":"object"},"name":"verify_document","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"embeddedReport":{"anyOf":[{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"allPassed":{"type":["boolean","null"]},"auditV2Overall":{"anyOf":[{"enum":["pass","pass_with_operator_decisions","review_required","unsafe","technical_fail"],"type":"string"},{"type":"null"}]},"blocking":{"type":["boolean","null"]},"carriesAuditReport":{"type":["boolean","null"]},"decisionChannel":{"type":["string","null"]},"inputSha256":{"type":["string","null"]},"licenseProvenance":{"anyOf":[{"additionalPropertie